## Issue / fix: fix(hg_state): avoid false-positive MERGING state

## Description
## Summary

`is_merge_state()` returns `io::Result<bool>`, but line 83 checked `.is_ok()` instead of inspecting the inner `bool`. This means `Ok(false)` (a non-merge repo) passed the check, causing every hg repo with a readable `.hg/dirstate` to display the MERGING state.

**Fix:** Replace `.is_ok()` with `.is_ok_and(|is_merge| is_merge)` so only `Ok(true)` triggers the merge label.

`is_ok_and` is stable since Rust 1.70 - no new dependencies needed.

Fixes #7322

