## Issue / fix: fix(aws): support `$duration` for `sso_session`

## Description
## Motivation and Context

Closes #7099

PR #6614 added support for displaying `$duration` for AWS SSO sessions, but only for the legacy format in which `sso_session` is not configured.

If not providing a session name, `aws configure sso` raises a warning.

```
WARNING: Configuring using legacy format (e.g. without an SSO session).
Consider re-running "configure sso" command and providing a session name.
```

It would be helpful to support SSO sessions because this is the format recommended by AWS.

## Description

This PR will add support for `$duration` when `sso_session` is present in the configuration for the selected AWS profile.

The implementation is based on the linked code from `botocore`.

https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/c0206cd0f53841190ec1f3c177272135f2284557/src/modules/aws.rs#L158-L159

The reason this doesn't work currently is that, if `sso_session` is present, the AWS CLI uses the _session name_ to compute the cache key, not the start URL. This PR will fix the implementation and update tests accordingly.

## How Has This Been Tested?

