## Issue / fix: fix: code being shifted when loaded via LDC

## Description
<!--
List the issues this PR closes (if any) in a bullet list format, e.g.:
- Closes #ABCD
- Closes #EFGH
-->

- Closes: #1502 

# Release notes

<!--
Use this only if this PR requires a mention in the Release
Notes Summary. Valuable features and critical fixes are good
examples. For everything else, please delete the whole section.
-->

In this release, we:

- fixed loader contracts not working when being called through a proxy contract
# Summary


The `IS` register is not going to point to the start of the loader code if it is loaded via `LDC`. Replaced that with the `PC` register value that should always point to the current instruction being executed.

