## Issue / fix: feat: certificate authentication for SFTP VFS provider

## Description
## Which issue does this PR resolve?

It adds yazi support for the ssh `CertificateFile` option, which allows users to authenticate using openssh certificates.
<!--
For any fixes and enhancements, we usually require an associated issue to be filed where clearly detailed your proposed changes and why they are necessary, which ensures we are aligned and reduces the risk of re-work.

You can use GitHub syntax to link an issue to this PR, such as `Resolves #1000`, which indicates this PR will resolve issue #1000.
-->


## Rationale of this PR

<!--
A clear and concise description of the rationale of the changes, to help our reviewers understand your intent and why it is necessary.

If it has already been detailed in the associated issue, please skip this section.
-->
This PR is pretty simple - it simply uses the `russh` functionality for certificates. Most of the code is just a copy which follows the same pattern as the public key option.

I added a `cert_file` option to the vfs configuration, and if it is set, it will load the certificate and use it for authentication.

There is also a `no_cert_verify` option, which can be used to skip certificate validation. For now, certificate validation isn't really implemented (verification would just be checking the certificate dates, and maybe the signature) as per the `russh` documentation, but it can be added. I just haven't really looked into how to get the CAs, etc.


