## Issue / fix: feat: new `sort_fallback` option to control fallback sorting behavior

## Description
An implementation of the feature request: #3064

Closes #3064 

---

This PR adds a `sort_fallback` option as the final tiebreaker when `sort_by` can't decide the order of files. For example:

```toml
sort_by = "extension"
sort_fallback = "alphabetical"
```

In this case, if two files have the same extension and their order can't be determined, it'll fall back to sorting by filename alphabetically, since filenames are unique.

`sort_fallback` has available values of `alphabetical` and `natural`, and only applies when `sort_by` is set to one of: `mtime`, `btime`, `extension`, or `size` where multiple files can have the same value of these attributes hence requires falling back.

